From: local
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: allow forcing the direct platform audio sink

createAudioSink() can run before the mediastream URI and source are attached,
so isMediaStreamPlayer() is not reliable at this point. Treat an explicit
WEBKIT_GST_MEDIASTREAM_DIRECT_AUDIO_SINK=1 as a force switch. Value 0 restores
the WebAudio provider wrapper, while an unset value keeps automatic detection.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@
     const char* directMediaStreamAudio = g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_MEDIASTREAM_DIRECT_AUDIO_SINK");
-    if (isMediaStreamPlayer() && (!directMediaStreamAudio || g_strcmp0(directMediaStreamAudio, "0"))) {
-        GST_WARNING_OBJECT(pipeline(), "Using direct platform audio sink for MediaStream playback");
+    bool useDirectAudioSink = directMediaStreamAudio
+        ? g_strcmp0(directMediaStreamAudio, "0")
+        : isMediaStreamPlayer();
+    if (useDirectAudioSink) {
+        GST_WARNING_OBJECT(pipeline(), "Using direct platform audio sink for playback (forced=%d)",
+            !!directMediaStreamAudio);
         return audioSink;
     }
